A Bachelor's Degree in Information Systems, Business Administration, Law, Production Engineering, Computer Science, or a related field is required.
Hands-on experience using and evaluating AI tools in a professional context (e.g., contract review automation, legal research, document drafting, workflow automation), with the ability to articulate how specific AI applications drive productivity, efficiency, and quality gains for a legal team across short-, medium-, and long-term horizons.
Prior experience working with Salesforce as a CRM/ CLM is a plus;
Good proficiency in Excel.
A minimum of 7 years of professional experience in roles with comparable scope and responsibilities (e.g., Legal Operations, legaltech, consultancy, or comparable Operations functions) is required, including at least 2 years spent directly managing or leading a team;
Hands-on evaluating, piloting, and implementing Legal Operations technology — including AI tools — with demonstrable examples of delivering or articulating productivity, efficiency, or quality improvements (e.g., AI Legal Technology, Contract Lifecycle Management, Litigation management system);
Experience in Legal Operations and/or at a legaltech, consultancy company or comparable experience in other Operations areas (e.g., Sales Ops, Finance Ops, Marketing Ops);
Experience with data visualization tools such as Tableau, Looker or Power BI;
Demonstrated, significant experience in large-scale, global project management and delivery.
Fluent English is mandatory.

Daily duties include, but are not limited to, assisting with the day-to-day support of our product:
Development of strategy and tactics for promoting the product on the Internet;
Development and implementation of marketing funnels;
Create posts for media, and newsletters;
Development of technical tasks for designers/programmers;
Competitive analysis.
Create an email-marketing growth strategy
Conduct Email tests for subject lines, copy, call to actions, etc
2+ years of experience working in marketing and/or project management
Proven successful experience in email marketing, targeting and social media marketing operations
Skills with a set of Google tools such as Google Analytics, Search Console, Tag Manager and the ability to analyze statistical information
Experience developing content for social media
Proven experience in identifying target audiences and in creatively devising and leading across channels marketing campaigns
Proficiency in Microsoft Office, Google and Adobe applications;
